================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
================================================================================

The MIT grant above covers everything in this repository, because no
third-party source file is vendored here. What the benchmark measures, and what
it merely refers to, are separated deliberately, and this section records which
is which.

1. Unlabelled external subset — benchmark/external/aws_samples/
   25 Terraform repositories published by AWS under the MIT No Attribution
   licence (MIT-0), identified in manifest.json by owner, name and full commit
   SHA. None of their content is copied into this repository. They are fetched
   on demand by experiments/fetch_external.py into .external-corpus/, which is
   gitignored, so this repository redistributes nothing of theirs and the MIT
   grant above extends to none of it. Each repository is governed by the licence
   in its own tree at the pinned commit. MIT-0 would have permitted vendoring;
   the reason for not doing so is provenance rather than licensing, and is set
   out in experiments/fetch_external.py.

2. CIS-mapped examples — benchmark/external/cis_examples/
   Four Terraform files, 42 lines in total, written for this benchmark to
   exercise controls named in the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark. Each carries a
   comment naming the control it exercises, for example "CIS AWS 2.1". No text,
   table, remediation step or other content from a CIS Benchmark document is
   reproduced here: a control identifier is cited, not copied. The CIS
   Benchmarks are published by the Center for Internet Security under its own
   terms, which govern the documents themselves and not this reference to them.
   The same applies to infrastructure/policies/cis_aws_benchmark.rego.

3. Catalogue records without files — benchmark/external/secureflag/ and
   benchmark/external/terraform_registry/
   These directories hold metadata.json only: case identifiers, expected
   verdicts and descriptions. The corresponding Terraform files are not present
   and are not distributed here, which is why the corpus report records 175
   externally declared cases against 4 actually loaded. That gap is reported
   rather than closed, and no measurement is attributed to a file this
   repository does not contain.

4. Tools under comparison
   Checkov, tfsec, Trivy, OPA and Terraform are invoked as external
   subprocesses and are not bundled, redistributed or derived from. Their
   versions are recorded in results/run_manifest.json. Each is governed by its
   own licence. Their recorded output under results/raw/ is factual observation
   of program behaviour.

5. Manuscript
   paper/ is typeset with Springer's svjour3 document class, which is not
   included in this repository and is obtained from the reader's own TeX
   distribution.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note on a licence that used to be here

Earlier revisions of this file carried a second licence, the Government Open
Data License – India (GODL-India), covering JSON and GeoJSON files derived from
the Local Government Directory of the Ministry of Panchayati Raj. Those files
belonged to a real-estate application that shared this repository and has since
moved to its own project; none of them produced any number reported here. The
GODL-India terms and their attribution requirement travelled with the data and
apply in that project, not this one. This is recorded so that anyone who
obtained those files under the old dual-licence text can see where the
obligation now lives.
